 by Natalia dire who many of  y'all know from stranger things is too  new to the art scene to have been  completely corrupted as an outsider  who's only just joining that world she's  still clear-headed enough to understand  what isn't art for example after  Gretchen bleeds to death from having her  arm sliced off by the sphere she's the  only person who can recognize that a  dead body sprawled on the floor isn't  actually a piece of art as artists  themselves John Malkovich's peers and  Debbie digs Tamra she seemed to  understand the underlying power of  deesis art peers and Amrish both become  mesmerized by Jesus paintings and this  seems to be the trigger that leads damn  rich to abandon read auras gallery and  go back to his collective much to  Josefina's disgust peers also goes back  to creating art purely for himself  making sand drawings that the tide  gradually washes away as the credits  roll interestingly enough that scene was  inspired by Dan Gilroy's own experiences  in the 1990s writing the movie Superman  live starring Nick Cage and directed by  Tim Burton when he found out the movie  was being canned after 18 months of hard  work Gilroy told II W that he went down  to the beach and thought about how  nothing he wrote was ever going to be  seen and so he might as well come down  and write words in the sand and have the  waves just wash them away but that was  also the day that Gilroy decided to  value what he creates not for how many  people see it or its commercial success  but simply for himself however you feel  about the movie velvet buzzsaw is more  than just a horror film set in the  contemporary art world it's also a  commentary about our relationship with  any art form including movies and TV but  wit buzz sauce producer Fox has said  it's about the commodification of art  and the way in which this self-selecting  group of curators and dealers is  anointing certain people ignoring other  people and creating a false economy  gilroys also said th